      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Throughput modes",
      "items": [
        "Elastic scales with usage and is the recommended default",
        "Provisioned pins a fixed value when you must guarantee steady throughput",
        "Bursting derives baseline throughput from stored capacity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Configuration caveats",
      "items": [
        "Every AZ needs a mount target and the security group must allow 2049/TCP",
        "Access points isolate POSIX permissions per directory, which is safer for multi-tenancy",
        "Lifecycle policies move cold files to the IA class to cut cost"
      ]
    }
